            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Divide the students of your class into three groups and ask each group to do one of the following activities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.208,
            0.902,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Collect the marks obtained by all the students of your class in Mathematics in the latest examination conducted by your school. Form a grouped frequency distribution of the data obtained."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.272,
            0.901,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Collect the daily maximum temperatures recorded for a period of 30 days in your city. Present this data as a grouped frequency table."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.316,
            0.901,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Measure the heights of all the students of your class (in cm) and form a grouped frequency distribution table of this data."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.361,
            0.902,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After all the groups have collected the data and formed grouped frequency distribution tables, the groups should find the mean in each case by the method which they find appropriate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.403,
            0.445,
            0.595,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "EXERCISE 13.1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.475,
            0.901,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A survey was conducted by a group of students as a part of their environment awareness programme, in which they collected the following data regarding the number of plants in 20 houses in a locality. Find the mean number of plants per house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.532,
            0.883,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
